From fb82f57a0175f64b2f2adbecd61cf7a8add55c57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:18:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: single-pass stereo VR for the 3D scenes

GA2_VR=1 (GA2_VR_STEREO=0 keeps theater mode): the GS stream goes to a
second paraLLEl-GS instance (own Vulkan device: Granite frame contexts are
per device and each renderer keeps a command buffer open) whose vertices
move by the right eye's parallax; the left eye's by the opposite (paraLLEl-GS
Hacks::stereo_shift_q, f * ipd/2 * Q). ga2_stereo carries the head pose and
shared field of view from ga2_vr to the game hooks (native/compat) and tags
each frame through the readback ring; ga2_vr shows each eye's frame full
view, submitted with the pose/FOV it was rendered with. Texture-pack images
are cached per device. GA2_VR_DUMP writes both eyes (no ImageFlipVertical on
a vector buffer); GA2_VR_DUMP_AT, GA2_VR_SCALE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
